PixelLab-generated sprites (SRD-CC)
===================================

These files are original Spellkave material generated with PixelLab. They are
not an inbound open-source grant. The Spellkave Proprietary License in the
repository root LICENSE file covers this original material. SRD 5.2.1 text
stays CC BY 4.0 under NOTICE; it is not relicensed here.

PixelLab output-rights finding (sk-jay0.3.5.14)
-----------------------------------------------

Retrieved: 2026-09-07
Current documented subscription: Tier 1 Pixel Apprentice (docs/design-assets.md).
PixelLab's public pricing URL https://www.pixellab.ai/pricing HTTP 308-redirected
to https://www.pixellab.ai/ on this date, so plan-specific commercial copy was
not readable. The Terms of Service do not carve output ownership by plan.

Sources (verbatim posture, not a paraphrase of a missing clause):

- Terms of Service: https://www.pixellab.ai/termsofservice
  Last Updated: 2025-11-23
- FAQ: https://www.pixellab.ai/docs/faq
  ("Can I use the generated images commercially?")
- Open RAIL-M (incorporated by ToS §4.1):
  https://github.com/CompVis/stable-diffusion/blob/main/LICENSE

Finding:

- Ownership: ToS §1.3 and §3.3 say the subscriber owns the copyrights in
  generated images and may use, modify, and distribute them for commercial
  and non-commercial purposes without PixelLab's permission.
- Attribution: the ToS and FAQ do not require crediting PixelLab on the
  published images.
- Commercial use: yes (ToS §1.3; FAQ: "Yes, we only ask that you do not
  train new models with the images.").
- Restriction (not ambiguous): do not train other models on the images
  without PixelLab's written permission (ToS §1.2, §3.3; FAQ).
- Additional bound: ToS §4.1 requires compliance with the linked Open
  RAIL-M text. This file does not restate that third-party license.
- Ambiguity: none on commercial use, ownership, or attribution for the
  published sprites. Plan-tier differences cannot be confirmed from the
  public pricing page as retrieved.

These sprites are therefore shippable as original Spellkave material under
the proprietary license, not as CC BY or any other OSS grant. Provider
output terms still apply (no model-training on the images). Bulk SRD
sprites (sk-jay0.3.5.6) still need a matching art/art-manifest.json entry
with sha256 before promotion; an empty tree is not a rights gap.
